{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01391",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 5.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the observations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.9,
      "end_seconds": 10.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.39,
      "end_seconds": 21.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, it's cramps in my calves at night. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.31,
      "end_seconds": 25.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.81,
      "end_seconds": 29.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "It's been two months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.52,
      "end_seconds": 33.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.24,
      "end_seconds": 36.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "I, I'd call it severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.79,
      "end_seconds": 40.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Alright, is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.7,
      "end_seconds": 49.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "It usually comes with trouble sleeping. The trouble sleeping? That's been for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.39,
      "end_seconds": 59.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.86,
      "end_seconds": 66.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "I've, I've had high blood pressure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.0,
      "end_seconds": 70.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "So, a few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.95,
      "end_seconds": 83.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.66,
      "text": "I swim twice a week. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.19,
      "end_seconds": 88.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Alright, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.08,
      "end_seconds": 94.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "So, nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.08,
      "end_seconds": 99.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.42,
      "end_seconds": 103.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.14,
      "end_seconds": 108.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.12,
      "end_seconds": 112.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.49,
      "end_seconds": 116.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.29,
      "end_seconds": 125.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.55,
      "text": "Losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day. I'm, I'm on magnesium tablets, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.7,
      "end_seconds": 130.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Have you had shortness of breath, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.35,
      "end_seconds": 134.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Definitely no shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.59,
      "end_seconds": 147.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "A few quick ones: weakness in the legs, swelling of the legs, redness of the leg or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.06,
      "end_seconds": 150.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Right, nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.68,
      "end_seconds": 155.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.93,
      "end_seconds": 159.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 173.92,
      "end_seconds": 183.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.22,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Blood pressure 109 over 68, saturation 98 percent. Temperature 36.6, heart rate 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.86,
      "end_seconds": 184.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.84,
      "end_seconds": 189.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.91,
      "end_seconds": 190.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.54,
      "end_seconds": 193.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.7,
      "end_seconds": 214.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Both calves are soft and not tender, and the pulses at your feet are good."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.18,
      "end_seconds": 217.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.24,
      "end_seconds": 225.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.8,
      "end_seconds": 250.99,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, my working impression is night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.7,
      "end_seconds": 253.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.55,
      "end_seconds": 285.47,
      "duration_seconds": 30.92,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like night-time muscle cramps without a worrying cause, but I'd like to confirm. I think a vitamin level makes sense here, for tingling feet. I want a blood sugar test done, that's for tingling feet. Gentle calf stretches against a wall before bed often help. Please don't wait if one leg becomes red, hot or swollen. That's when to be seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.3,
      "end_seconds": 290.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.18,
      "end_seconds": 293.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Yes, that's manageable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.62,
      "end_seconds": 297.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.2,
      "end_seconds": 301.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}